ng\",\n","    \"I like eating pizza\"\n","]\n","\n","# Generate embeddings\n","embeddings1 = model.encode(sentences1)\n","\n","# Calculate cosine similarity\n","similarity1 = cosine_similarity(embeddings1)\n","\n","print(similarity1)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"ad3c480d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.511543Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.511129Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.517781Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.516783Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020894,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.519802+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.498908+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["I love machine learning  <->  I enjoy coding = 0.43828994\n","I love machine learning  <->  I like eating pizza = 0.24764907\n","I enjoy coding  <->  I like eating pizza = 0.3782606\n"]}],"source":["# similar sentences\n","\n","for i in range(len(sentences1)):\n","    for j in range(i + 1, len(sentences1)):\n","        print(\n","            sentences1[i],\n","            \" <-> \",\n","            sentences1[j],\n","            \"=\",\n","            similarity1[i][j]\n","        )"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e5e5fcef","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010291,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.540685+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.530394+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Why do we need embeddings?**\n","\n","Consider these sentences:\n","\n","1. How can I develop an AI application?\n","2. How do I build an artificial intelligence system?\n","3. What is the capital of Bangladesh?\n","\n","The first and second sentences have similar meanings, even though their words are different.\n","\n","Traditional keyword search may struggle to identify that relationship.\n","\n","Embedding models represent semantic relationships numerically, allowing a vector search system to retrieve relevant information."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"a28f18be","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.563597Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.563213Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.59448Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.59321Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045661,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.59693+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.551269+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[[1.         0.7258661  0.07632804]\n"," [0.7258661  1.0000001  0.0169613 ]\n"," [0.07632804 0.0169613  1.        ]]\n"]}],"source":["sentences2 = [\n","    \"How can I develop an AI application?\",\n","    \"How do I build an artificial intelligence system?\",\n","    \"What is the capital of Bangladesh?\",\n","]\n","\n","# Generate embeddings\n","embeddings2 = model.encode(sentences2)\n","\n","# Calculate cosine similarity\n","similarity2 = cosine_similarity(embeddings2)\n","\n","print(similarity2)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"18af024c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.62019Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.619793Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.626427Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.62542Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020796,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.628627+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.607831+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["How can I develop an AI application?  <->  How do I build an artificial intelligence system? = 0.7258661\n","How can I develop an AI application?  <->  What is the capital of Bangladesh? = 0.07632804\n","How do I build an artificial intelligence system?  <->  What is the capital of Bangladesh? = 0.016961299\n"]}],"source":["# similar sentences\n","\n","for i in range(len(sentences2)):\n","    for j in range(i + 1, len(sentences2)):\n","        print(\n","            sentences2[i],\n","            \" <-> \",\n","            sentences2[j],\n","            \"=\",\n","            similarity2[i][j]\n","        )"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b7f8bb55","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010849,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.650593+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.639744+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Vector Database\n","\n","When you generate embeddings, you typically store them in a database along with the original sentence.\n","\n","Each sentence gets converted into a numerical vector by your embedding model.\n","\n","## What exactly does a vector database store?\n","\n","A vector database typically stores more than just vectors.\n","\n","It stores three important things:\n","\n","1. Vector embeddings.\n","2. Original data or a reference to the original data.\n","3. Metadata.\n","\n","For example, imagine you are building a RAG application for technical documentation.\n","\n","A record might look like this:\n","\n","```py\n","{\n","    \"id\": \"doc_001\",\n","    \"text\": \"FastAPI is a Python web framework.\",\n","    \"embedding\": [\n","        0.21,\n","        0.45,\n","        0.78,\n","        0.12\n","    ],\n","    \"metadata\": {\n","        \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\",\n","        \"page\": 12,\n","        \"category\": \"programming\",\n","        \"author\": \"OpenAI\"\n","    }\n","}\n","```\n","\n","Let's understand each field.\n","\n","| Field     | Purpose                              |\n","| --------- | ------------------------------------ |\n","| ID        | Uniquely identifies a record         |\n","| Text      | Original content                     |\n","| Embedding | Numerical representation             |\n","| Metadata  | Additional information for filtering |\n","\n","**Why store metadata?**\n","\n","Imagine a user asks:\n","\n","> Explain FastAPI authentication from the official documentation.\n","\n","You can search semantically while filtering:\n","\n","```py\n","filter = {    \n","    \"category\": \"programming\",\n","    \"source\": \"fastapi_documentation.pdf\"\n","}\n","```\n","\n","This allows you to combine semantic search with traditional filtering.\n","\n","## How data looks in a database\n","\n","| id | sentence | embedding | metadata |\n","|---|---|---|---|\n","| 1 | I love machine learning | `[0.21, 0.45, 0.78, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"AI\", \"source\": \"doc1.pdf\"}` |\n","| 2 | Python is a programming language | `[0.32, 0.12, 0.89, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"programming\", \"source\": \"doc2.pdf\"}` |\n","| 3 | Artificial intelligence is fascinating | `[0.56, 0.23, 0.67, ...]` | `{\"category\": \"AI\", \"source\": \"doc3.pdf\"}` |\n","\n","The embedding column stores the entire vector (for example, 384 floating-point values), not just the first and last five values.\n","\n","## Embeddings using SQLite\n","\n","### Store Embeddings\n","\n","SQLite is a simple database that you can use to understand how embedding storage works."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"8e16377d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.673458Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.67303Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.752788Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.751849Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.093759,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.754881+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.661122+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\n","All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\n","All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\n"]}],"source":["\n","import sqlite3\n","import json\n","\n","# Connect to database\n","conn = sqlite3.connect(\"embeddings.db\")\n","cursor = conn.cursor()\n","\n","# Create table\n","cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sentences (\n","    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n","    sentence TEXT,\n","    embedding TEXT,\n","    metadata TEXT\n",")\n","\"\"\")\n","\n","# Generate and store embeddings\n","for i, sentence in enumerate(sentences1):\n","\n","    embedding = model.encode(sentence2)\n","\n","    # Create metadata\n","    metadata = {\n","        \"category\": \"AI\",\n","        \"source\": \"document.pdf\",\n","        \"page\": i + 1\n","    }\n","\n","    cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n","        INSERT INTO sentences (sentence, embedding, metadata)\n","        VALUES (?, ?, ?)\n","    \"\"\", (\n","        sentence,\n","        json.dumps(embedding.tolist()),\n","        json.dumps(metadata)\n","    ))\n","    print(\"All sentences successfully stored in SQLite!\")\n","\n","conn.commit()\n","conn.close()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"948013c2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010595,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.776181+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.765586+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Here:\n","\n","- `sentence` stores the original text.\n","- `embedding` stores the vector as a JSON string.\n","- `embedding.tolist()` converts the NumPy array into a Python list.\n","- `json.dumps()` converts that list into a string for SQLite storage.\n","\n","### Retrieve Embeddings\n","\n","Now let's retrieve the stored vectors.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"7e07832c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.799608Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.798671Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.807745Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.80681Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.022821,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.80966+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:24.786839+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["ID    | Sentence                            | Embedding                                     | M