or similarity |\n","| Converts text into vectors | Compares vectors |\n","| Generates numerical representations | Generates similarity scores |\n","\n","## BM25 (Best Matching 25)\n","\n","BM25 is a ranking algorithm widely used in modern search engines and hybrid retrieval systems.\n","\n","It improves upon traditional TF IDF by considering:\n","\n","1. Term frequency.\n","2. Inverse document frequency.\n","3. Document length normalization.\n","4. Term frequency saturation.\n","\n","The BM25 formula is:\n","\n","$$\n","\\begin{aligned}\n","BM25(D,Q)=\\sum_{t\\in Q}&IDF(t)\\\\\n","&\\times\n","\\frac{f(t,D)(k_1+1)}\n","{f(t,D)+k_1(1-b+b\\frac{|D|}{avgdl})}\n","\\end{aligned}\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","| Parameter | Meaning |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| $D$ | Document |\n","| $Q$ | Search query |\n","| $f(t,D)$ | Frequency of term in document |\n","| $IDF(t)$ | Inverse document frequency |\n","| $\\|D\\|$ | Document length |\n","| $avgdl$ | Average document length |\n","| $k_1$ | Controls term frequency saturation |\n","| $b$ | Controls document length normalization |\n","\n","Typical values are:\n","\n","- $k_1 = 1.2$ to $2.0$\n","- $b = 0.75$\n","\n","### Why BM25 is better than basic TF IDF\n","\n","Imagine two documents:\n","\n","- D1: `Vector database` (2 words)\n","- D2: `Vector database` repeated 50 times in a long document.\n","\n","A basic term frequency approach might give D2 an excessively high score because the query terms appear many times.\n","\n","BM25 uses term frequency saturation, meaning that repeating a term 50 times does not necessarily make the document 50 times more relevant.\n","\n","It also normalizes for document length, helping avoid unfairly favoring longer documents.\n","\n","In vector databases: BM25 is particularly useful for retrieving documents that contain exact keywords, technical terms, product names, identifiers, or specific phrases."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":26,"id":"32aebcc1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execu