| Complexity | Simple | More advanced |\n","| Ranking quality | Good baseline | Often better |\n","\n","Remember:\n","\n","- TF IDF = How important is a word in a document?\n","- BM25 = How relevant is a document to a query using BM25 scoring?\n","- Cosine Similarity = How similar are two document/query vectors?\n","\n","This distinction is fundamental to understanding how keyword search and semantic search work.\n","\n","# Semantic Searching\n","\n","This is probably the most important mathematical concept behind vector databases.\n","\n","When you search for something, the database needs to determine which stored vectors are closest to your query vector.\n","\n","There are several similarity and distance metrics.\n","\n","The three most important are:\n","\n","1. Cosine similarity\n","2. Euclidean distance (L2)\n","3. Dot product (inner product)\n","\n","Let's understand each one.\n","\n","![Semantic Searching](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/semantic_searching.png)\n","\n","## Cosine similarity\n","\n","Cosine similarity measures the angle between two vectors.\n","\n","It tells us how similar the directions of two vectors are.\n","\n","The formula is:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Cosine Similarity}(A,B)= \\frac{A\\cdot B}{||A||\\\\.||B||} $$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $A$ = Query vector.\n","- $B$ = Stored vector.\n","- $A\\cdot B$ = Dot product.\n","- $||A||$ = Magnitude (length) of vector A.\n","- $||B||$ = Magnitude of vector B.\n","\n","Let's use a simple example.\n","\n","Suppose:\n","\n","$$ A=[1,2] $$\n","\n","$$ B=[2,4] $$\n","\n","First, calculate the dot product:\n","\n","$$ A\\cdot B=(1\\times2)+(2\\times4) $$\n","\n","$$ =2+8=10 $$\n","\n","Calculate the magnitude of A:\n","\n","$$ ||A||=\\sqrt{1^2+2^2} =\\sqrt{5} $$\n","\n","Calculate the magnitude of B:\n","\n","$$ ||B||=\\sqrt{2^2+4^2} =\\sqrt{20} $$\n","\n","Now:\n","\n","$$ \\text{Similarity}= \\frac{10}{\\sqrt5\\times\\sqrt{20}} $$\n","\n","$$ =\\frac{10}{10}=1 $$\n","\n","Similarity = 1.0\n","\n","This means the vectors have exactly the same direction.\n","\n","### Understanding cosine similarity values\n","\n","| Score | General interpretation     |\n","| ----- | -------------------------- |\n","| 1     | Same direction             |\n","| 0.9   | Very similar direction     |\n","| 0.7   | Somewhat similar direction |\n","| 0     | Perpendicular directions   |\n","| -1    | Opposite directions        |\n","\n","These are geometric interpretations, not universal semantic similarity thresholds. The meaning of a score depends on the embedding model and dataset."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":33,"id":"f7ff8db6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.27345Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.273076Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.277811Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.276915Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.026865,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.279994+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.253129+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["A = embeddings2[0]\n","B = embeddings2[1]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":34,"id":"5563ee9c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.315211Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.314856Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.321102Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.31992Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.026359,"end_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.323223+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T06:33:51.296864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[-0.00912357 -0.05206461 -0.00902052 -0.04356401 -0.03594175] [ 0.09292182  0.01521754  0.12191691 -0.00579256  0.00519618]\n","[ 0.04651576 -0.03570966  0.00531281 -0.06252249 -0.04663933] [ 0.02544288  0.00252984  0.06603173  0.04685618 -0.0144894 ]\n"]}],"source":["print(A[:5], A[-5:])\n","print(B[:5], B[-5:])"]},{"c